# ( dp/dPsi )( Psi ) for examples/q-driven.toml, against the SOURCE's normalised
# flux -- one on the axis, zero at the plasma boundary.
#
# CONSTANT, deliberately. The point of that example is the outer loop on the
# TOROIDAL field, so the pressure half is held as simple as it can be: a
# constant dp/dPsi contributes mu0 r^2 * 0.45 to F and nothing that varies with
# Psi, which leaves every change between outer iterations attributable to gg'.
#
# Mu0 = 1 in that file, so this is in the same normalised units as the rest of
# it and is not a pascal per weber.
#
#        Psi              dp/dPsi                  d2p/dPsi2
   0.000000            0.450000000              0.000000000
   1.000000            0.450000000              0.000000000
